# Equinox framework extension, no launcher and no weaving. Equinox reads hookconfigurators.properties
# from the class loader that loaded org.eclipse.osgi, once, while the framework is being constructed
# (HookRegistry.mergeFileHookConfigurators). The jar therefore belongs on the -runpath; installed as a
# bundle it would be inert, because that scan is long over by then. Not a bundle.
Bundle-Description: ServiceLoader mediator as an Equinox framework extension: registry from \
	META-INF/services (and module-info provides), installed as a ClassLoaderHook through \
	hookconfigurators.properties. No launcher, no bytecode weaving, no mediator metadata.

# own package plus the private copies of the shared core and the Equinox hook
-privatepackage: \
	org.example.spi.equinox,\
	org.example.spi.mediator.equinox,\
	org.example.spi.core

# lives in the framework class loader; OSGi imports are meaningless here
Import-Package:
-jpms-module-info: ,
-sources: false
-noextraheaders: true
